Z||000002||thomas_l||09-06-2001||10:42 AM||||I have watched PayPal get less and less "friendly" with their terms. For that matter, any third party currency exchange is going to pork you. My suggestion would be to open a US bank account (use an Internet bank) to channel PayPal funds or other US transactions. When you do cash transactions from the US bank to your home bank you shouldn't get screwed too bad on the exchange.<P>One of the high points of my trip to Canada last month was my $100 ATM withdrawls showed up on my account as $66. Now if I could get that from the local ATMs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
